# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# Where a file is installed decides how it runs.  The clock in
# apps/trusted is LOADED into this process and is already showing when
# the desktop opens; the sketch beside it is a row that starts in a
# process of its own when chosen.  Neither was linked into anything.
wait 25
note the folder window opened over it; the clock was there first
key w ctrl
wait 6
note the trusted application is already open, without being asked for
click-window Clock
wait 4
expect-title Clock
click 980 20
wait 4
expect-menu Editor|Sketch|Terminal
note choosing one that is not trusted starts it through the runner
menu-pick Sketch
wait 110
expect-title Sketch
key Escape
wait 20
expect-no-title Sketch
